<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>Sheetwright</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Sheetwright</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="Package">
    <PackageId>Sheetwright</PackageId>
    <Description>A small, MIT-licensed .xlsx writer over DocumentFormat.OpenXml. Styles, number formats, data validation, tables, defined names, pictures, freeze panes and auto-fit — plus a streaming writer for exports too large to hold in memory — with an API shaped like the one you already know from EPPlus, and no commercial licence.</Description>
    <PackageTags>xlsx;excel;spreadsheet;openxml;export;csv;streaming</PackageTags>
    <!--
      Shown on nuget.org beside the version. Kept to what changed, in the same
      words as CHANGELOG.md, because a release note that restates the package
      description tells a reader nothing about whether to upgrade.
    -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
Added: SpreadsheetStreamWriter, a single worksheet written straight to a stream one row at a time, for an export too large to hold in memory. SpreadsheetPackage keeps every cell until it is asked for the bytes, which is what lets styles merge and columns auto-fit, and what runs a worker out of memory on a report of several hundred thousand rows. The streaming writer keeps nothing but the row in hand, and the bytes reach the destination as the rows arrive. A table on a streamed sheet may be left open at the bottom — pass null for its last row and it ends at the last row written.

Fixed: NaN and the infinities are written as text rather than as numbers. The file format has no numeric spelling for any of the three, so a numeric cell holding NaN produced a workbook Excel offered to repair rather than open.

Changed: a streamed table and a table on an in-memory sheet resolve their column names through the same code, so an empty heading becomes its column letter and a repeated one gains a suffix identically in both.

Full notes: https://github.com/sinanoran/sheetwright/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <!--
      CS1591 is off while the public surface is documented incrementally. The
      types that carry a comment carry a real one; turning this into an error
      today would buy fifty stubs saying "Gets or sets the value".
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="DocumentFormat.OpenXml" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Sheetwright.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
